==Latvian==
{{slim-wikipedia|kivi (putni)|kivi (1)|lang=lv}}
[[File:Tokoeka.jpg|250px|thumb|Kivi (1)]]
{{slim-wikipedia|kivi (auglis)|kivi (2)|lang=lv}}
[[File:Kiwi_aka.jpg|thumb|250px|Kivi (2)]]

===Etymology===
Via other European languages, ultimately a {{borrowing|mi|kiwi|lang=lv|nocap=1}}, originally an [[onomatopoeic]] imitation of the bird's call. Originally the name of the bird, the English word [[kiwi]] soon became a term for people and things from [[New Zealand]], and was thus also used, initially as a brand name, for the fruit, which is also from [[New Zealand]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{lv-IPA|kivi}}
{{audio|lv-riga-kivi.ogg|lang=lv}}
* {{lv-IPA|kiviː}}
{{audio|lv-riga-kivi-2.ogg|lang=lv}}

===Noun===
{{lv-noun|m|-}}

# [[kiwi]] [[bird]] {{gloss|a [[flightless]] [[bird]] ([[genus]] ''Apteryx'') [[find|found]] only in [[New Zealand]]}}
#: '''''kivi''' dzimta'' — '''kiwi''' family (''Apterygidae'')
#: '''''kivi''' ir putni, kas dzīvo tikai Jaunzēlandē'' — the '''kiwi''' are birds that live only in New Zealand
# [[kiwi fruit]] {{gloss|a [[Chinese gooseberry]] [[vine]] [[fruit]] of the [[genus]] ''Actinidia'' with [[hairy]] [[brown]] [[skin]] and [[dark]] [[green]] [[flesh]]}}
#: '''''kivi''' ir subtropu auglis ar brūnu, pūkainu mizu un zaļu mīkstumu'' — the '''kiwi''' is a subtropical fruit with brown, hairy skin and green flesh
#: '''''kivi''' pēc formas atgādina olu'' — the '''kiwi''' is shaped like an egg

====See also====
* {{l|lv|aktinīdija}}

